<DocsLayout lang="en" title="Welcome to Quira" description="Documentation for Quira Browser — a local-first browser that transforms your browsing into a queryable knowledge graph." section="Getting Started" headings={headings}>

  <h1 id="welcome-to-quira" class="content-section">Welcome to Quira</h1>

  <p>Quira is a local-first browser that transforms your browsing activity into a structured, queryable knowledge graph. Unlike traditional browsers that treat tabs as disposable, Quira automatically captures the context of your research — what you read, how topics connect, and where your investigation left off — so you can ask your browser anything and get answers grounded in your own experience.</p>

  <p>This documentation covers everything you need to get started with Quira, understand its core concepts, build on its APIs, and contribute to its development.</p>

  <Callout type="tip" title="New to Quira?">
    <p>Start with the <a href="/docs/en/getting-started/quick-start/">Quick Start</a> guide to get up and running in under 5 minutes, then explore <a href="/docs/en/core-concepts/context-graph/">Core Concepts</a> to understand how Quira structures your browsing context.</p>
  </Callout>

  <hr>

